Error [E2417]: explicit failure domain ``E`` is not an Error type
  --> tests/ui/fallible_ignored.jet:5:8
    |
  5 | fn f() Int !E -> Ok(1)
    |        ^^^^^^
 Why: A `!` contract may name `Err`, a Core error, a type marked `#Error`, an all-error union, or `Never`; arbitrary value types do not describe failures.
 Fix: use a Core error, add `#Error` to a local error type, or remove the explicit error contract.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2417

Error [E2402]: `?` can't convert `AllocError` into `Err` — no declared conversion exists
  --> tests/ui/fallible_ignored.jet:9:8
    |
  9 |     xs.try_push(2)
    |        ^^^^^^^^
 Why: `?` uses the declared conversion rail; `AllocError` can reach `Err` only through `impl AllocError -> Err`
 Fix: add `impl AllocError -> Err { … }` before this function, or change the return type
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2402
